From 691a81d5f548fa57bc7d27279cb0c0f9f4ce51be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: flashnext-hybrid <hybrid@flashnext.local>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 09:23:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] port the flashnext series onto the qwen4exp/mtp-fix lineage

Re-ports, adapted to this lineage:
- device-resident recurrent snapshots, extended to the separated PLE conv row
  (p_l) and sized from the live tensors; K-slot rollback writes in
  build_conv_state_at (fixes BOTH conv rows); QWEN4EXP on the rs-rollback
  allowlist. Upstream's replay/no-reverify and distribution acceptance kept.
- uniform draft length for co-batched multi-sequence verification, integrated
  with adaptive drafting (uniform overrides per-sequence lengths when more
  than one sequence drafts, or split_equal shreds the batch again).
- QSA top-k gather, dispatched inside build_attn_qsa with the producer sizing
  in build_qsa_top_k; helpers in llama-graph. Value-rotation unwind preserved.
- GDN output-projection flatten and expand-late for qwen4exp (25748619d and
  eb3d32a6c covered qwen35/qwen35moe/qwen3next but not this arch).
Dropped as already present here: can_reuse, LDS stride pad, grouped MTP hnorm.

Measured on the Q4 model, interleaved against the unpatched branch, PLE on
disk in both arms:
  PAR=1: 33.6 -> 50.6 tok/s (+50.6%), acceptance equal or better
  PAR=4: 42.1 -> 83.4 tok/s (+98%)
  65K needle with the gather active: 3/3, byte-identical answers
  700-token correctness probe (rollback incl. the PLE row): ALL PASS
